Z||000000||Philphine||03-12-2001||11:35 AM||||<BR>i'm hoping to get my gt chin spoiler in a few weeks for the gt nose i'm putting on my '87 coupe. i've also just started trying to repair the nose on the '84 chop top. both will sit really low and i'm thinking of ways to protect them as best i can. i'm meaning to start looking to see if they even make them anymore.<P>for you young guys curb feelers look like cellular phone antennas that you put on the rocker panel near the wheels that you were supposed to hear scrape before you hit your tire on the curb. if you don't remember electra 225's (deuce anna quartah) you might not have heard of them. the last time i tried them was about 6 years ago trying to protect some driving lights that sat really low.i usually had my stereo up too high and couldn't hear them anyway. in this case they'd sit in front facing forward at the bottom of the nose. <P>probaly would'nt even be considered ricey.<P>it'd be pimpy.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)<BR>'84 chop top (parts car or project. time will tell)||||reg||1
