Z||000005||Alex4mula||03-12-2001||01:38 PM||||What about an electronic proximity sensor? K-mart sells a garage Parking sensor that have  green-yellow-red lights that change as you get near it. You program the distance. I don't think it is accurate enough for the application but it may work and maybe could be modified for your purpose. It uses 4 AA batteries and cost about $40.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Philphine||03-12-2001||05:06 PM||||allright already...i knew that would draw comments from the peanut gallery, but i may still try it. i mean, if i really can get some protection out of it, why not. they're pretty much screw on things, so if i don't get anything out of it or i can't live with the ridicule i can take them off.<P>1fst, not putting the chevy in my sig is kind of a knee jerk reaction to not wanting to be considered the stereotype corvette owner. i guess thats as much in my head as real. i don't have any cute vette shirts, car stickers that say my other car is a vette, and i don't talk about it much. there are a few people who know me but are surprised when they see me in the car. so i have no problem putting my fieros in my vette forum sig but i didn't put the vette in my sig here. it's pretty much a project too. nothing to draw much attention when i'm in it.<P>just a peek into my flicked thinking.||||reg||1
