Z||000008||rogergarrison||03-12-2001||07:39 PM||||a friend of mine bought some steel wheeled roller skates at a garage sale, cut them in half and bolted that to each side of front frame so they were just slighly lower thanfront air dam. If you do hit anything like a steep drive or speedbump, rolls right over it with no damage and they dont show at all. Could prob use some steel toolbox wheels from like Home Depot too.||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||03-13-2001||08:06 PM||||If you really want to have some fun..... you can obtain an ultrasonic ranging unit based on Polaroid's camera setup. There are a number of robotics and electronics places that should have it. It will measure from about a foot to 18 feet as I recall. This is esentially the system used on the ford? van... Once upon a time Polaroid even had a "developer kit" that sold for around a $100. <P>In reality.... No matter how careful you are it will get broken sooner or latter. The skate idea isn't bad. ||||reg||1
